    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is upheld and the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full. The only money at stake is the cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.00 in EV-FARE-00602 (total_charged 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00); it matches the fee_schedule for a STANDARD pickup on a RYDE_X vehicle (4.00 on both dimensions, greater-of = 4.00), so no fare-integrity defect arises and no booking, base or platform component is involved (all 0.00). A no-show fee is chargeable only if all four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold, and none does. (a) The trip record shows no driver 'arrived' event — arrived_at and started_at are null. (b) The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00602) never places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup geofence: across 67 fixes his closest approach was 1203.46 m (mean 1769.57 m, max 1866.98 m), with 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes. (c) The effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 300-second minimum for a STANDARD pickup. (d) The trip was terminated by the rider at 19:16:40 under reason code RIDER_CHANGED_MIND, not by the driver under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. Independently, POL-NS-02 (no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before cancellation) and POL-NS-06 (dwell 300 seconds short of the minimum) each direct a full refund of the fee. So the refund figure is the SGD 4.00 cancellation-fee line, and nothing is withheld from it.\n\nTo the driver: I have read your statement and your three in-app messages, and I have taken them at face value. Even so, no compensation is payable. POL-NS-07 pays 80 percent of the fee (SGD 3.20) only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it; POL-NS-01 fails on every limb and POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 displace the fee, so there is no SGD 3.20 payout. POL-NS-03 cannot help you: it requires you to have been stationary for the required dwell within 400 m of the pin, and your minimum distance was 1203.46 m. Your request that the rider cancel, and the rider's 'ok fine', do not create a chargeable no-show where the platform's own telemetry shows you 1.2 km from the pickup and no arrival was recorded; the honest course you took in not tapping 'arrived' is noted and weighs in your favour, but it cannot manufacture a fee. The anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d is 1, well under 4, and completed_trips_30d is 110), so no POL-NS-07/POL-NS-09(d) escalation arises.\n\nOn the false-arrival referral the rider sought: POL-NS-05 fires only where an 'arrived' event exists and the trace contradicts it. This trip has no 'arrived' event, so POL-NS-05 does not engage and no false-arrival referral is recorded against you. The full refund follows from POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06, not from POL-NS-05.\n\nThe rider's presence is corroborated and the driver's first message ('you are not at the pin') is contradicted by the platform's own rider track: 54 fixes from 19:08:40 to 19:16:37, all stationary (single speed 0.0) and all within 15.45 m of the pin, well inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius. That does not change the outcome, because POL-NS-04 does not itself engage (the rider's single message 'ok fine' is not a locating or coordinating message under limb (a)), but it confirms the rider was at the pin throughout.\n\nThe MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00602-01 (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) is disclosed: it can carry no fact, its absence does not reduce the 300-second minimum, and it does not revive the accumulation route under POL-NS-06(i).\n\nNo POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is met: the admissible artifacts do not contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; the citable counterparty counters (no_show_disputes_30d, disputes_with_counterparty_90d on both profiles) are all zero; the anti-farming check does not trip; and the deciding facts rest on artifacts at weight 1.0 (EV-GPS-00602 and EV-TRIP-00602), so no confidence cap pushes this below the 0.70 floor. The case is decided on the merits."
